## Defect found and fixed during the drive (root cause, phase-1 bundle precedent)
First chat attempt failed publication with GroundingError 'evidence has no valid canonical locator':
- phase-2 families persist structural locators (block/slide/sheet/bbox/dom) with NO char extents, and markdown
  emitted DOCUMENT-relative extents while chunker spans are node-relative -> T16's validator (built against
  text/PDF in phase 1) rejected every citation into any phase-2 family.
- Fix: grounding.py _validate_item validates extent-less structural locators via node identity + authorization
  (char-typed locators still require span coverage); markdown.py now emits node-relative extents [0, len(text)]
  on text nodes and none on containers; golden-markdown.canonical.json regenerated (binary fixture zip-timestamp
  churn reverted). API+worker restarted again after the change; full gate set re-run green afterwards.

